From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] [CUDA] Add explicit host-mapped buffer annotations

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-commit: fd5305807b09d447eb8fb89fa10c553cb69a9498

Rationale: Zero-copy CPU mapped pinned buffers passed into TileLang kernels previously failed device residency checks or triggered misleading device index lookups in the Cython and tvm_ffi adapters. Add T.annotate_host_mapped_buffers(...) to validate CU_MEMORYTYPE_HOST + CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_IS_MANAGED/MAPPED via cuPointerGetAttribute and allow annotated host-mapped tensors alongside GPU tensors.

Quality: Opt-in annotation; no change to unannotated kernel launches.

Tests: testing/python/jit/test_tilelang_jit_host_mapped.py across cython and tvm_ffi backends across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from tile-ai/tilelang#3802 (commit fd5305807b09d447eb8fb89fa10c553cb69a9498).
